workflow:







      ukoserver_Provision
      Provision a UKO Server
    1.0.0.0
      IBM

          5655-EKM
          UKO
          V2R1+
          ukoserver






	&variables;
    &variables_users;


        Define users and groups
        Create the required z/OS user IDs and groups for UKO server operation. This includes technical users for Liberty server processes, UKO-specific users for key management roles, and optionally a certificate client user for testing and integration purposes.

        &step_define_users_liberty;
        &step_define_users_uko;




        Define key rings and certificates
        Set up the security infrastructure by creating SAF key rings and digital certificates. This includes the server certificate for TLS communication, OpenID Connect (OIDC) certificate for authentication, trust certificates for external systems, MSDKE certificates if Microsoft Double Key Encryption is required, and optionally client certificates for mutual TLS authentication.

        &step_define_keyring;
        &step_define_keyring_oidc;
        &step_define_keyring_trust;
        &step_define_keyring_msdke;




    &step_define_database;


    &step_define_server;


        Use the provided start command to bring up the server
        This step provides the start command to bring up the provisioned server on z/OS using started task.
            You have to manually issue this command on the z/OS console to bring up the provisioned server.


            Start the server with the following start z/OS console command:



            START ${instance-SERVER_STC_NAME}




            Verification After start, the address of your server is:



            https://${instance-SERVER_HOSTNAME}:${instance-SERVER_PORT_TLS}



        1
        System
        true
        false
